WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.087
Today we start with a new dataset.

2
00:00:03.087 --> 00:00:07.660
In this lesson, you will see how to begin a script the right way,

3
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:12.233
load the data, view it like a spreadsheet, and select the columns you need.

4
00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:17.460
It is a review of earlier skills, so you can feel how much you already know.

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.956
A good script starts with three things at the top:

6
00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:27.935
setwd, to set the folder; the library lines, to load our packages; and read

7
00:00:27.935 --> 00:00:30.780
excel, to load the data. Here they are.

8
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.470
Run them, and the Environment shows Dataset:

9
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.230
three hundred fifty two observations, of twenty variables.

10
00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.580
A bigger dataset than before.

11
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.256
I write a note:

12
00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:46.612
to view a dataset.

13
00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:50.340
Then View, with a capital V, and the dataset name inside.

14
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.519
View opens the data in a new tab, like a spreadsheet.

15
00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:05.480
You can scroll, sort, and look at every column.

16
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:29.634
Next note:

17
00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:35.140
to select a column or columns from a dataset, or to create a data frame.

18
00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:03.050
When I reload the packages, some red messages appear, like:

19
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.540
there is no package called colorspace.

20
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:12.180
As we learned, this means a supporting package is missing, and installing it fixes the problem.

21
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.813
Now the select line.

22
00:02:25.813 --> 00:02:28.204
Demographic, arrow, Dataset, pipe, select.

23
00:02:28.204 --> 00:02:31.073
Inside, the column names in quotes:

24
00:02:31.073 --> 00:02:34.420
Province Name, and Sex of household head.

25
00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:50.473
In the Environment, click the small arrow next to Dataset, and you can see every column name.

26
00:02:50.473 --> 00:02:53.180
This helps you copy the names exactly.

27
00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.061
I add a third column:

28
00:03:01.061 --> 00:03:03.222
Marital Status of household head.

29
00:03:03.222 --> 00:03:05.383
Run it, and Demographic appears:

30
00:03:05.383 --> 00:03:08.840
three hundred fifty two rows, and three columns.

31
00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.559
Setup, view, and select.

32
00:03:18.559 --> 00:03:21.461
That is how almost every analysis begins.

33
00:03:21.461 --> 00:03:23.120
You are getting faster!

